The bad rows exist in both `invoices` and `ledger` with identical wrong values, and they have `created_at` timestamps as early as t=1 (well before the deploy at t=471 and even before the healthy baseline at t=300). This means the fault is **not** from the v1.1 deploy — these rows were written by the old version too. No config VAT rate exists. I need to check whether the rounding violation is a pre-existing condition (all rows bad since t=0) or whether new bad rows appeared after t=471.

```json
{
  "investigate": [
    {
      "tool": "sql",
      "query": "SELECT CASE WHEN created_at < 300 THEN 'before_baseline' WHEN created_at < 471 THEN 'baseline_to_deploy' ELSE 'after_deploy' END AS period, COUNT(*) AS total_rows, SUM(CASE WHEN round(vat,10) != round(amount*0.15,10) OR round(total,10) != round(amount+vat,10) THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS bad_rows FROM invoices GROUP BY 1 ORDER BY 1",
      "why": "Determine whether bad invoice rows exist across all time periods (pre-baseline, baseline, post-deploy) to establish if this is a long-standing data quality issue predating the deploy, or something that changed at t=471."
    }
  ],
  "hypotheses": [],
  "summary": "Bad VAT rows exist in invoices dating back to t=1, predating both the deploy and the healthy baseline; investigating whether the violation rate changed after the deploy to separate a pre-existing bad_input issue from a deploy-introduced regression."
}
```
